 "notes": "Defects of the original kept (behaviour unchanged, commented in the code):\n- BLINK-MISTAKE moves X'F1' to MSGA (the attribute byte: autoskip + MDT) instead of the highlight byte.\n  This is the program's own deliberate demonstration. Fix: MOVE DFHBLINK TO MSGH.\n- CHECK-INPUT never tests WS-RESP after RECEIVE MAP (fact \"unchecked_responses\", field-tested).\n  On MAPFAIL, HXM2I stays LOW-VALUES and ACCTL = 0, so the task sends \"ACCOUNT MUST BE 6 DIGITS\".\n  Fix: IF WS-RESP = DFHRESP(MAPFAIL) resend the first-entry screen.\n- AMOUNT is never validated; its NUM attribute only restricts the keyboard. When AMOUNT is not\n  entered, AMOUNTI stays LOW-VALUES. Those X'00' bytes then go into MSGO through the STRING, and\n  back out as AMOUNTO on the DATAONLY send.\n  Fix: IF AMOUNTL = 0 MOVE ZEROS TO AMOUNTI before the STRING.\n\nModelling notes:\n- HXM2O REDEFINES HXM2I. On both CHECK-INPUT sends, ACCTO and AMOUNTO therefore carry the received\n  ACCTI / AMOUNTI data. Received data is modelled as BMS lays it out:\n  - ACCT uses JUSTIFY=(LEFT,BLANK).\n  - AMOUNT uses JUSTIFY=(RIGHT,ZERO).\n  - ACCTL is the length of the value typed.\n  - A field that is null or empty is treated as not received: length 0, LOW-VALUES.\n- Hxm2Screen carries no received flag bytes (ACCTF / AMOUNTF / MSGF). On the CHECK-INPUT sends,\n  AMOUNTA and MSGA keep whatever flag BMS set (X'80' after an erase-EOF). They are ported as not\n  set, i.e. LOW-VALUES. On the error path ACCTA is overwritten.\n- EIBCALEN = 0 is tested as !task.hasCommarea(), or eibcalen() == 0.\n\nFacts contradicted: none found. The screen_bindings, calls, commarea_contracts and cics_resources\nfacts (field testing open) all match the source.",
